---
import Signup from './Signup.astro';
import ArchFigure from './ArchFigure.astro';
---
<section class="section final" aria-labelledby="final-title">
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="section-rule"></div>
    <h2 id="final-title" class="display h2 c-text" data-reveal>Start from what you already know.</h2>
    <p class="lede c-text final-lede" data-reveal>Join the early-access list, and we’ll write when your invitation is ready.</p>
    <div class="c-text final-form"><Signup id="email-bottom" /></div>
    <figure class="c-note final-fig">
      <ArchFigure kind="final" />
      <figcaption class="note">
        <span class="smallcaps">Fig. 3.</span> Archimedes measuring a circle: hexagons inside and
        outside it, their sides doubled four times, to 96. That was enough to show that π lies
        between 3&#8239;<span class="frac">10/71</span> and 3&#8239;<span class="frac">1/7</span>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .final-lede { margin-top: calc(var(--u) * 2); }
  .final-form { margin-top: calc(var(--u) * 4); }
  .frac { font-variant-numeric: diagonal-fractions; }
  .final-fig { margin-top: calc(var(--u) * 6); max-width: 240px; }
  .final-fig figcaption { margin-top: calc(var(--u) * 2); }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    /* the form row takes any extra height from the figure, so the heading,
       lede and form keep their spacing */
    .grid { grid-template-rows: auto auto auto 1fr; }
    .final-fig { grid-row: 2 / span 3; align-self: start; margin-top: 0; max-width: 280px; }
  }
</style>
